.\" Man page for the Arsenal platform CLI.
.\" Kept in lock-step with the argparse subcommands by cli/tests/test_manpage.py.
.TH ARSENAL 1 "2026-07-05" "Arsenal" "Arsenal Manual"
.SH NAME
arsenal \- white-hat security platform CLI (Arsenal live OS)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B arsenal
.RI [ global-options ]
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ command-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B arsenal
is the platform command for the Arsenal white-hat security operating system
(Arch Linux + BlackArch). With no
.I command
it prints the
.BR armory ,
the registry that maps a memorable weapon name to the real tool it launches.
Other subcommands provide health and security diagnostics, safe updates,
support bundles, and guided engagement workflows.
.PP
Each check the platform performs is designed to run unprivileged and degrade
gracefully; commands that perform active testing require the caller to confirm
authorization.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the Arsenal version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable coloured output (also honoured via
.BR ARSENAL_NO_COLOR ).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose logging to stderr.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B armory " [\fIQUERY\fR] [\-\-installed|\-\-missing] [\-\-json]"
List the weapon registry (weapon \(-> tool \(-> category \(-> description).
A filled dot (\(bu) marks tools present on the image. An optional
.I QUERY
filters by name, tool, category, or description (case-insensitive);
.B \-\-installed
and
.B \-\-missing
filter by whether the tool is present on this image;
.B \-\-json
emits a machine-readable inventory. This is the default when no command is given.
.TP
.B doctor " [\-\-json]"
System health and security diagnostics: hardened kernel, AppArmor, nftables
default-deny, kernel-hardening sysctls, blacklisted modules, network exposure,
updates, integrity, and more. Exit status is non-zero only if a check fails.
.B \-\-json
emits the results for monitoring or scripting.
.TP
.B update " [\-\-check] [\-y] [\-\-no\-snapshot]"
Refresh repositories and upgrade packages safely (keyrings first, snapshot
prepared for rollback).
.B \-\-check
lists pending updates only;
.B \-y
skips the prompt;
.B \-\-no\-snapshot
skips the Timeshift hook. The upgrade itself requires root.
.TP
.B reportbug " [\-\-no\-redact] [\-o \fIFILE\fR]"
Collect a compressed support bundle (logs, hardware, packages, services).
Sensitive data is redacted by default.
.TP
.B report
Generate or manage engagement reports from recorded workflow runs.
.TP
.B engagements " [list|show|rerun|delete|archive] [\fIDIR\fR]"
Manage recorded engagement projects under
.IR ~/engagements :
list them, show one, re-run its workflow (with the authorization prompt),
archive it to a tarball, or delete it.
.TP
.B recon " \fITARGET\fR"
Recon workflow: port/service scan plus web content discovery against an
authorized target.
.TP
.B web " \fITARGET\fR"
Web workflow: server misconfiguration and injection checks, with a Burp
hand-off, against an authorized target.
.TP
.B ad " \fITARGET\fR"
Active Directory workflow: authenticated enumeration and attack-path mapping
against authorized hosts.
.TP
.B profile
Manage package/tooling profiles (e.g. full vs. lean toolkits).
.TP
.B ai " [\fIPROMPT\fR ...]"
Ask the built-in AI assistant (optional; degrades gracefully when no provider
is configured).
.TP
.B dashboard
Show a consolidated status dashboard for the live system.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/arsenal/registry
The weapon registry \(em single source of truth for the armory and the
.I /etc/profile.d
launchers.
.TP
.I /var/log/arsenal/arsenal.log
Platform CLI log.
.TP
.I /etc/sysctl.d/99-arsenal-hardening.conf
Kernel-hardening sysctls verified by
.BR "arsenal doctor" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List only the web weapons:
.B arsenal armory web
.TP
Machine-readable health for a monitor:
.B arsenal doctor \-\-json
.TP
See what is pending without changing anything:
.B arsenal update \-\-check
.SH AUTHORS
The Arsenal project.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nft (8),
.BR aa-status (8),
.BR pacman (8)
.PP
Full documentation ships under
.I /usr/share/doc
and in the project repository.
